<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juliana of the Netherlands</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1909">1909</a>–<a href="/years/2004">2004</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Queen Juliana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juliana was Queen of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> from 1948 to 1980, succeeding her mother Wilhelmina. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> she lived in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. Her reign saw the transfer of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> in 1949, post-war reconstruction and the growth of the welfare state, and her informal style made the monarchy popular. She abdicated in 1980 in favour of her daughter Beatrix.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/juliana-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="Juliana of the Netherlands" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Max Koot · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Queen_Juliana,_1973.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
